   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to hunting in Seneca county; and to amend chapter 73 of the laws of 2015 amending the environmental conservation law relating to authorizing hunting in the county of Seneca, in relation to making such provisions permanent",
    "basePrintNo": "S6025",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6025-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0907, En Con L; amd §2, Chap 73 of 2015",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6025\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the environmental conservation law,\nin relation to hunting in Seneca county; and to amend chapter 73 of\nthe laws of 2015 amending the environmental conservation law relating\nto authorizing hunting in the county of Seneca, in relation to making\nsuch provisions permanent\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis bill would make permanent provisions permitting the use of rifles\nfor big game hunting in Seneca County.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSections 1 through 3 amend the Environmental Conservation Law to\npermanently permit the use of rifles for big game hunting in Seneca\nCounty.\n\nSection 4 contains the effective date.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nChapter 73 of 2015 permitted the hunting of big game through the use\nof a rifle in all of Seneca County until October 1 2017.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Seneca County Board of Supervisors, by Resolution NO. 14-17\nadopted on February 14, 2017, has requested the New York State\nLegislature to enact legislation, that will allow the permanent use of\nrifles for big game hunting in all of Seneca County. Rifles have been\nsuccessfully used for the past two big game hunting seasons in Seneca\nCounty. This legislation is necessary to allow the permanent use of\nrifles for big game hunting in all of Seneca County.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that\nsections one and three of this act shall take effect upon the\nexpiration and reversion of paragraph a of subdivision 2 of section\n110907 of the environmental conservation law, as provided in section\n13 of chapter 600 of the laws of 1993, as amended.\n",
